/-- **The theorem of the virtual-root certificate WY5.** Let `x` be nine unit vectors of `ℝ⁴` and `(e, f)` an
orthonormal pair such that the configuration lies in the piece of the certificate (`CAP.VR.InPieceS`: the
identities of the frame, the inequalities of the cell lemma with the constants of the certificate, the guards,
the intervals of the record types and the bounds for the deviations). Then the energy
`∑ i < j, 1 / ‖x i - x j‖ ^ 2` exceeds `35 / 2`. -/
theorem energy {x : Fin 9 → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)} {e f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4)}
    (h : CAP.VR.InPieceS par heads x e f) :
    (35 : ℝ) / 2 < ∑ i, ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j => i < j), 1 / ‖x i - x j‖ ^ 2 := by
  exact lt_of_eq_of_lt (by norm_num) (CAP.VR.energy_gt labels_ok checked bound_ok h)

end T8V.WY5

